# kex: check-only
# A module whose header does not match its file's place under the source
# root is found under neither name. `using` the declared name used to build
# with the module silently left out, and the first call failed at run time
# with "Unknown module" or "Undefined function". The build now says where the
# module is and what its path makes it.
using Misplaced.Authority

main do
  IO.printLine(granted?("admin"))
end
